<article class="env-definition" id="84BF8E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/84BF8E">Definition <span data-tag="84BF8E">6.3.1.6</span>.</a>fibration!topos A map $p: X \rightarrow S$ of simplicial sets is a <em>topos fibration</em> if the following conditions are satisfied: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The map $p$ is both a Cartesian fibration and a coCartesian fibration. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
For every vertex $s$ of $S$, the corresponding fiber $X_{s} = X \times _{S} \{ s\} $ is an $\infty $-topos. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(3)$"><p>
For every edge $e: s \rightarrow s'$ in $S$, the associated functor $X_{s} \rightarrow X_{s'}$ is left exact. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>